{"id":"word:hebrew:H1605","type":"word","title":"גָּעַר","subtitle":"H1605 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"to chide","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to גָּעַר (H1605) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 14 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"גָּעַר (gâʻar) means to chide First listed occurrence: Gen 37 10."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"גָּעַר","transliteration":"gâʻar","pronunciation":"gaw-ar'","strong":"H1605","lemmaId":"hebrew:H1605","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["וַ/יִּגְעַר","וְ/גָ֥עַר","וּ/מִ/גְּעָר","גָעַ֔רְתָּ","גֹעֵ֤ר"],"morphs":[["HVqp2ms",3],["HC/Vqw3ms",2],["HVqrmsa",2],["HC/Vqq3ms",1],["HC/R/Vqc",1],["HC/Vqq1cs",1],["HVqv2ms",1],["HVqi2mp",1],["HVqj3ms",1],["HC/Vqj3ms",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"to chide","usage":"corrupt, rebuke, reprove.","full":"H1605. gaar גָּעַר verb rebuke (Aramaic גְּעַר id., Ethiopic cry out , Sabean יגער proper name, SabDenkm p. 29.30 ) — Isa 17:13 ; גָּעַרְתָּ Psa 9:6 2 t., etc.; Imperfect יִגְעַר Zech 3:2-3 t., תִּגְעֲרוּ Ruth 2:16 ; Imperative גְּעַר Psa 68:31 ; Infinitive מִגְּעָרֿ Isa 54:9 ; Participle גּוֺעֵר Nahum 1:4 , גֹּעֵר Mal 2:3 ; &#8212; with בְּ except Psa 9:6 ; 68:31 ; 119:21 ; Mal 2:3 where accusative; — 1 rebuke , father his son Gen 37:10 (E), reapers Ruth Ruth 2:16 , priest Jeremiah Jer 29:27 . 2 of God rebuking nations Psa 9:6 ; Isa 17:13 , proud Psa 119:21 , Satan Zech 3:2 (twice in verse), קנה חית Psa 68:31 , בָּאֹכֵל (the devouring swarm of locusts, restraining them) Mal 3:11 , the sea drying it up Psa 106:9 ; Nahum 1:4 , Zion Isa 54:9 ; הַזֶּרַע the seed (prevent the usual harvest) Mal 2:3 ( ᵐ5 Aq הַזְּרֹעַ ᵑ9 , the arm , namely, of priests, that they may not extend it to bless).","rootNote":"a primitive root;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"Gen 37 10","keyReferences":["Gen 37 1